# Release procedures of an invented project [SPEC:DOC-RELEASE-PROCEDURES]

## [DEC-SIGNED-RELEASE-TAGS] Release tags are signed

- statement: every release tag is a signed tag made with the release maintainer's key
- rationale: a downstream packager can verify that a release came from the project
- invalidating-assumption: the project's users verify signatures; if none do, the step costs more than it protects

## [INV-TESTS-PASS-BEFORE-TAG] No release tag on a failing suite

- statement: a release tag is never made on a commit whose full test suite has failed

## [PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN] Release from the main branch

- trigger: the maintainers agree that the main branch is ready to ship a new version
- owner: release maintainer
- status: active
- tools: the test runner; version control with signed tags; the package index upload command
- must-not: publish from a working copy with uncommitted changes
- last-reviewed: 2026-10-29
- implements: [DEC-SIGNED-RELEASE-TAGS]
- depends-on: [INV-TESTS-PASS-BEFORE-TAG]

### [STEP-RUN-TESTS] Full test run

- part-of: [PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN]
- actor: release maintainer
- action: run the full test suite on a clean checkout of the release commit
- next-step: [STEP-TESTS-GREEN]

### [STEP-TESTS-GREEN] Test result check

- part-of: [PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN]
- actor: release maintainer
- action: read the test summary
- condition: the suite reports zero failures
- if-true: [STEP-SIGN-TAG]
- if-false: [STEP-FAILURE-REPORT]

### [STEP-SIGN-TAG] Signed release tag

- part-of: [PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN]
- actor: release maintainer
- action: create a signed tag named after the new version on the tested commit
- next-step: [STEP-PUBLISH]

### [STEP-PUBLISH] Package upload

- part-of: [PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN]
- actor: release maintainer
- action: upload the built package for the tagged commit to the package index

### [STEP-FAILURE-REPORT] Failure report, no tag

- part-of: [PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN]
- actor: release maintainer
- action: make no tag; file an issue naming the failing tests and the commit

## [PROC-HOTFIX-RELEASE] Hotfix release

- trigger: a defect in the released version needs a fix before the next planned release
- owner: release maintainer
- status: draft
- must-not: include changes that are not part of the fix
- last-reviewed: 2026-03-02
- depends-on: [INV-TESTS-PASS-BEFORE-TAG]

## [MATRIX-WHICH-RELEASE-PROCEDURE] Which release procedure to follow

- question: which procedure does a given release need
- rule: read the rows in order and follow the first whose need matches
- row-1-need: a fix for a defect in the released version, with nothing else
- row-1-use: PROC-HOTFIX-RELEASE
- row-2-need: a new version from the main branch
- row-2-use: PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN
- row-3-need: anything else
- row-3-use: no release; raise it with the maintainers
- see-also: [PROC-HOTFIX-RELEASE]
- see-also: [PROC-RELEASE-FROM-MAIN]
